{
  "sourcePatchId": "94a7c447-e728-4e30-8c5c-9e6e3d57ffc0",
  "name": "The Real TB303",
  "description": "Sawtooth TB-303 bass. MIDI velocity selects flags, without continuous velocity gain: 1-63 normal; 64-95 slide; 96-111 accent; 112-127 accent + slide.\nPerformance controllers (read by new notes):\n- Env Mod: 0-1 linear, default 0.6. Filter sweep = envelope * Env Mod * 4000 * (0.4 + accentFlag * Accent * 0.4).\n- Decay (s): 0.03-3 seconds logarithmic, default 0.3. Controls only the separate filter envelope; amplitude decay remains 0.3 seconds.\n- Accent: 0-1 linear, default 1. Scales accented-step filter and iamp boosts together; 0 removes both boosts. iamp = 0.4 + accentFlag * Accent * 0.5.\n- iamp / Drive: 0.1-32x logarithmic, default 1x; multiplies iamp before tanh. Post-tanh compensation (1 + 0.025 * drive) / (1.025 * drive) limits level changes; this is a fixed curve, not a loudness limiter.\n- Slide: 0.1-2x linear, default 1x. Multiplies portk half-time: 60 ms for slide, 1 ms for regular notes at 1x.\nAll new defaults preserve the original sound. Existing controller IDs and settings are retained.\nMIDI CC10: cutoff 40-16000 Hz logarithmic (49 approximately 404 Hz); CC11: resonance 0-0.98 (114 approximately 0.88). Both follow the played MIDI channel with 10 ms smoothing.\nSlide retains prior voice state. Use a single-note line, start with a non-slide note, and leave at least 50 ms after note-off for voice reuse. Overlapping/release-tail voices do not share pitch history; this is native portk, not a legato note-priority engine.\nRoute Stereo Output through the performance mixer to Master.",
  "isTemplate": false,
  "alwaysOn": false,
  "instrumentType": "bass",
